  <!-- ========== 3. 24-48H DELTA ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>President Trump stated on September 9 that the war with Iran would end "immediately after the midterm elections" on November 3, telling reporters in Dallas that Tehran was artificially prolonging the conflict to drive up fuel prices and damage him politically. Neither Iran's Foreign Ministry nor the Supreme National Security Council issued a response to the statement. The IAEA Board of Governors voted 23-7 the same day to refer Iran to the UN Security Council — the first such referral in 20 years — following a resolution co-sponsored by the United States, Germany, France and the United Kingdom. → supports <span class="cite">F3</span> without move</p>
      <p>US CENTCOM announced on September 5 that its forces had struck three Iranian crude oil carriers in the Persian Gulf after the IRGC launched ballistic missiles at two US Navy warships (CNN, Sep 5; ABC News, Sep 8). A second exchange followed on September 10, when Iranian forces — in an operation Trump described aboard Air Force One as Iranian-directed — hit US aircraft at the Al-Tanf garrison in Jordan. Both the September 5 tanker strikes and the September 10 Jordan attack are confirmed by US military statements. → moved <span class="cite">F2</span></p>
      <p>FM Araghchi conducted a telephone call with Pakistan army chief Gen. Asim Munir on September 10; Pakistani officials characterized the exchange as a message-relay coordination meeting, not a negotiating session (Reuters, Sep 10). President Pezeshkian's government restated on September 1 that Iran would return to the June memorandum if the United States did the same (Spectrum News / Euronews, Sep 1), but Araghchi's August 19 position — demanding "a complete end to the war" rather than a ceasefire — remained the dominant framing in Iranian state media through the reporting period. → moved <span class="cite">F3</span></p>
      <p>Haaretz published a Channel 12 survey on September 8 showing Eisenkot's Yashar party at 25 seats and Likud at 21 — the widest seat gap since the campaign registered. Channel 13 and Kan published separate polls showing Eisenkot leads of 22/21 and 24/21 respectively. Eisenkot's prime ministerial suitability rating reached 52% against 38% for Netanyahu — a 14-percentage-point gap that Channel 12 and Channel 13 each recorded as a new high. War management was cited as the top electoral issue by 32% of Channel 12 respondents. → moved <span class="cite">F5</span></p>
      <p>Straits.live recorded 6 commercial transits through the Strait of Hormuz on September 6, against a pre-war baseline of 85 per day; 418 vessels continued holding position offshore as of that date. US declared the strait mine-free in late August (Axios, Aug 25), but maritime advisories remained at "SEVERE" and the September 5 IRGC missile attack on US warships confirmed continued Iranian naval operational activity. Trump's September 9 statement deferring any deal to after November left no observable diplomatic precursor for a commercial shipping recovery before October 3 or October 31. → moved <span class="cite">F4</span>, <span class="cite">F7</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

