      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path (22%):</strong> Near-term IRGC attack (F2=55%) sustains the kinetic exchange; IAEA UNSC referral (Sep 9) opens a Chapter VII escalatory pathway; containment requires US restraint that has been inconsistent since September 1.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (65%):</strong> Trump's midterm framing locks the conflict at current exchange intensity through November; no diplomatic channel operates at held-session level; Hormuz transit recovering at &lt;10/day; both sides retain electoral incentives to maintain the status quo through November 3.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (13%):</strong> A mediator-confirmed session (F6=15%) or a Saudi-channel breakthrough are the only observable green shoots; Pezeshkian's conditional memorandum offer (Sep 1) is the sole available Iranian diplomatic signal.</p>
    </div>
